 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "can / can't (능력)",
   "en": "can / can't (ability)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "can은 '~할 수 있다'는 능력을 나타내요. 모든 주어에 같은 can을 쓰고 동사는 원형을 씁니다: She can swim (not cans, not swims). 부정은 can't, 질문은 Can + 주어 + 동사?로 만듭니다.",
   "en": "Can shows ability. It stays the same for every subject and the verb stays in the base form: She can swim (not cans, not swims). The negative is can't and a question is Can + subject + verb?"
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "주어 + can + 동사",
     "I can swim."
    ],
    [
     "can't",
     "I can't drive."
    ],
    [
     "Can + 주어 + 동사?",
     "Can you cook?"
    ],
    [
     "대답",
     "Yes, I can. / No, I can't."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "can 뒤에는 동사 원형: She can swim.",
    "en": "After can use the base verb: She can swim."
   },
   {
    "ko": "he / she에도 can (cans 아님).",
    "en": "Even with he / she it is can (not cans)."
   },
   {
    "ko": "can과 can't는 발음이 달라요. can't는 더 강하게 들려요.",
    "en": "Can and can't sound different; can't is stronger."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "I can swim.",
    "ko": "저는 수영할 수 있어요."
   },
   {
    "t": "She can cook well.",
    "ko": "그녀는 요리를 잘할 수 있어요."
   },
